# MCP Inspector — Usage (no install required)

The MCP Inspector runs via **npx** without requiring installation. See: [modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/tools/inspector](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/tools/inspector).

## Run the Inspector

```bash
npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector <command>
npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector <command> <arg1> <arg2>
```

## Inspect servers from npm

```bash
npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/inspector npx <package-name> <args>
# Example:
npx -y @modelcontextprotocol/inspector npx @modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem /Users/username/Desktop
```

## Inspect servers from PyPI

```bash
npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector uvx <package-name> <args>
# Example:
npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector uvx mcp-server-git --repository ~/code/mcp/servers.git
```

## Inspect locally developed servers

**TypeScript:**
```bash
npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector node path/to/server/index.js args...
```

**Python:**
```bash
npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector \
  uv \
  --directory path/to/server \
  run \
  package-name \
  args...
```

Read the server’s README for exact run instructions.

## Features

- **Server connection pane** — Choose transport, set command-line args and environment for local servers.
- **Resources tab** — List resources, metadata (MIME, descriptions), inspect content, test subscriptions.
- **Prompts tab** — List prompt templates, test with custom arguments, preview messages.
- **Tools tab** — List tools, view schemas, test with custom inputs, view results.
- **Notifications pane** — Server logs and notifications.

## Best practices

1. **Start** — Launch Inspector with your server; verify connectivity and capability negotiation.
2. **Iterate** — Change server → rebuild → reconnect Inspector → test; monitor messages.
3. **Edge cases** — Test invalid inputs, missing prompt args, concurrent ops, error handling.

